WEBVTT

00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:11.625
Fight! Something or another!

00:00:11.625 --> 00:00:13.542
I am in a situation where
the crisis is so dangerous

00:00:13.542 --> 00:00:15.458
that I don't have time to be
saying things like that!

00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:17.375
No, seriously! Really!

00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:20.750
And so, anybody there?!

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.750
I'm gonna give permission...

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.625
If there is someone...

00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:27.500
To turn Excel Saga...

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.583
Help me, damn it!

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:31.667
Into a survival drama!

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:35.000
What's the deal with
that self-absorbed echo!

00:00:35.792 --> 00:00:37.792
Why?!

00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:40.333
Do you feel better now?

00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:43.333
Here you go, a chuu-chuu
ice bottle as a reward.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.167
Drop!

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:01.583
<i>Sore wa ai ja nai</i>

00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:05.500
<i>Ai wa sore ja nai</i>

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:13.375
<i>Aishite iru kedo aisarete wa inai</i>

00:01:13.375 --> 00:01:17.292
<i>Kesshite ai ja nai</i>

00:01:17.292 --> 00:01:21.375
<i>Ketsu wa ai ja nai</i>

00:01:21.375 --> 00:01:29.042
<i>Aisaretai keredo motometari wa shinai</i>

00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:33.875
<i>Kono mi sasagete inochi nagedashi</i>

00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:37.833
<i>Wakime mo furazu tada hitasura ni</i>

00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:41.750
<i>Damashite sukashite yokohairi</i>

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.042
<i>Tanin o fumitaoshi keri o kamashite</i>

00:01:45.042 --> 00:01:47.125
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:01:47.125 --> 00:01:49.042
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.875
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:52.875
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>

00:01:52.875 --> 00:01:57.708
<i>Banana no kawa de korondemo</i>

00:01:57.708 --> 00:02:00.833
<i>Sore wa subete ano kata no tame</i>

00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:05.333
<i>Shiite iu nara sore wa kitto</i>

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:13.167
<i>Ai to iu na no chuuseishin</i>

00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:21.208
"Kyushu International Airport"
"(here)"

00:02:32.542 --> 00:02:33.500
<i>Sutchii</i>...

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.958
Flight attendant.

00:02:34.958 --> 00:02:36.625
But you're a <i>Sutchii</i>, aren't you?

00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:38.375
Flight attendant!

00:02:38.375 --> 00:02:40.125
Make it <i>Sutchii </i>for me!

00:02:40.125 --> 00:02:41.833
--Hey, wait! Metallic things are...
--Flight attendant!

00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:42.500
--Hey, wait! Metallic things are...
--But you're a <i>Sutchii</i>, aren't you?!

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.500
--But I don't have any.
--But you're a <i>Sutchii</i>, aren't you?!

00:02:53.792 --> 00:02:55.792
Camera, why did you stop?

00:02:55.792 --> 00:02:58.125
I'm not a criminal.

00:02:58.125 --> 00:03:00.500
This isn't an adult video either!

00:03:05.125 --> 00:03:08.667
Don't cut an introductory
scene short. You got it?

00:03:11.375 --> 00:03:12.375
"For the television staff.
Koshi Rikdo’s character notes."

00:03:12.375 --> 00:03:13.125
"Misaki Matsuya"

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.250
"Gender: Female  Age: 22 yrs"

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:14.792
"A character that does not flatter her guests"

00:03:14.792 --> 00:03:15.292
"A quarter British"

00:03:15.292 --> 00:03:15.750
"Hobbies: Traveling alone"

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.292
"Family: Parents, younger brother"

00:03:16.292 --> 00:03:16.792
"First Person Reference: Atashi"

00:03:16.792 --> 00:03:17.292
"Second Person Reference: Anata"

00:03:17.292 --> 00:03:18.833
"Uses “kun” to scoundrels"

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.000
Quit giving yourself airs
and making low-cost animation!

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.042
"Sorry..."
"Director"

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.667
"City Hall"

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:32.417
So, my memorable first day of
going to work has finally come!

00:03:32.417 --> 00:03:35.250
Today, now,
from this moment forth,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.417
I will guard the peace of this
city with this very hand!

00:03:39.417 --> 00:03:42.792
What's he getting all worked up
about becoming a civil servant?

00:03:42.792 --> 00:03:43.625
"What a simple guy..."

00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:48.042
Good morning! Starting today,
I will be working--

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.500
So, this is the way it's gonna be,
right from the first day.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.458
"Pretend we're strangers..."

00:03:56.458 --> 00:03:58.458
That's the only way to go.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.333
Watanabe, Sumiyoshi, help me.

00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:06.042
Damn it, let go,
you damn stranger!

00:04:06.042 --> 00:04:07.625
You won't get away!

00:04:07.625 --> 00:04:08.708
No!

00:04:08.708 --> 00:04:09.958
"Department of City Environment Security"

00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:12.542
This is it? Is this really the place?

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.000
"Nice expansive layout..."

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.083
More like, isn't this
an unnecessarily big room?

00:04:21.542 --> 00:04:24.375
If you can't speak properly,
just shut your mouth!

00:04:24.375 --> 00:04:27.917
<i>How did a guy like this get</i>
<i>to be a civil servant anyway?</i>

00:04:27.917 --> 00:04:29.875
<i>Getting accepted along with this thing</i>

00:04:29.875 --> 00:04:32.708
<i>is going to lower</i>
<i>people's opinion of me too!</i>

00:04:32.708 --> 00:04:36.292
<i>Anyway, I've finally gotten</i>
<i>a stable job in this recession.</i>

00:04:37.708 --> 00:04:39.708
"Take a look at this."

00:04:41.125 --> 00:04:42.250
"Written orders"?

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.917
The first day will be
used for orientation training.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.875
"It says it's a secret order."

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:49.583
What I was looking for was...

00:04:54.292 --> 00:04:56.542
Mr. Watanabe, it is truly wonderful

00:04:56.542 --> 00:05:00.917
that you found a secure job,
even in this recession.

00:05:00.917 --> 00:05:04.958
Not at all. I did it all so that
I could free you from poverty.

00:05:04.958 --> 00:05:07.333
Oh, my. For me?

00:05:07.333 --> 00:05:09.833
I will take care of you
for the rest of your life.

00:05:09.833 --> 00:05:11.000
I'm all yours.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.458
And so you shall be.

00:05:13.083 --> 00:05:15.917
That's enough of that
emotional stuff on your own!

00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:17.167
Take that! Take that! Take that!

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:18.667
Oh, my dream...

00:05:21.583 --> 00:05:24.333
Though our strategy
last time was a success,

00:05:24.333 --> 00:05:28.833
the ignorant masses still do not see
how the world really should be.

00:05:28.833 --> 00:05:31.292
The ideal society exists!

00:05:31.292 --> 00:05:32.792
It exists here!

00:05:33.792 --> 00:05:36.792
That is why I dare say

00:05:36.792 --> 00:05:42.292
that this city belongs to us,
the ideological organization ACROSS!

00:05:42.292 --> 00:05:44.042
This is not a possibility,

00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:47.292
but a definite conclusion that
will come about in the near future!

00:05:47.292 --> 00:05:49.375
Hail, Ilpalazzo!

00:05:49.375 --> 00:05:50.833
...zzo...

00:05:50.833 --> 00:05:55.083
It's a little weird, but I like
starting out the standard way.

00:05:55.083 --> 00:05:56.750
Do you think--

00:05:58.292 --> 00:06:00.292
And here she dies again!

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.083
In any case,

00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:06.125
though the path to establishing
an ideal society is a long journey,

00:06:06.125 --> 00:06:08.667
the time that has
been allotted to us is limited.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.542
If we forget to take
a step forward every day,

00:06:10.542 --> 00:06:12.500
that journey could even become infinite!

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:15.042
What is the thing that
we need most right now?

00:06:15.042 --> 00:06:16.375
What?

00:06:17.333 --> 00:06:18.833
Is it money?

00:06:19.833 --> 00:06:22.042
The circulating currency
with no substantial value,

00:06:22.042 --> 00:06:24.375
created by the current corrupt society,

00:06:24.375 --> 00:06:26.583
is unnecessary to our ACROSS.

00:06:27.333 --> 00:06:29.833
What do we need?
That answer is resources!

00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:31.667
Acquiring resources is what is necessary

00:06:31.667 --> 00:06:33.958
for us to successfully realize our ideal!

00:06:33.958 --> 00:06:35.917
It is the greatest
condition we must meet!

00:06:35.917 --> 00:06:38.917
Well, even if we have
resources, our personnel is...

00:06:38.917 --> 00:06:41.042
You are truly great,
Lord Ilpalazzo!

00:06:41.042 --> 00:06:43.042
What we need is resources!

00:06:43.042 --> 00:06:46.292
It is what a certain great man
from a country in the East said!

00:06:46.292 --> 00:06:47.875
He said that with mineral resources,

00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:49.708
they could fight on
for another ten years!

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:52.208
Though they lost in the end anyway.

00:06:53.542 --> 00:06:56.250
Did I get something wrong?!

00:06:59.083 --> 00:07:00.875
"I don't really care,
but aren't we there yet?"

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.375
Yeah.

00:07:02.375 --> 00:07:05.458
This is really far for being the
city's in-service training center.

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:07.375
Are you saying there's
a problem with my navigation?

00:07:07.375 --> 00:07:07.792
"F City, F Prefecture"

00:07:07.792 --> 00:07:09.250
"F City, F Prefecture"
"Maybe this was all they could afford."

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:13.375
But still, it's already
been five hours since we left.

00:07:13.375 --> 00:07:14.583
What is it?

00:07:14.583 --> 00:07:15.917
I see.

00:07:16.625 --> 00:07:19.000
We should've turned right
on that road just now after all.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.208
Just now? There hasn't
been any turns for a long time now.

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:24.458
Remember? That fork in the
road that we passed after lunch.

00:07:24.458 --> 00:07:26.708
Why you! That's not just now!

00:07:26.708 --> 00:07:28.917
We're already two prefectures away!

00:07:28.917 --> 00:07:31.583
My neck! My neck, my neck!

00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:39.583
Oh, hello. Excel here.

00:07:39.583 --> 00:07:42.417
It's ridiculously cold. I'm on
the verge of freezing to death.

00:07:42.417 --> 00:07:44.250
What I am doing here

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:46.417
is working to collect
gold dust from the river

00:07:46.417 --> 00:07:48.917
in order to acquire resources.

00:07:48.917 --> 00:07:51.250
It is all for Lord Ilpalazzo!

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:54.750
Resources! Resources!
You must obtain resources!

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.875
Yes, Lord Ilpalazzo!

00:07:56.875 --> 00:07:58.500
The only problem is that

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.417
no one has ever heard of
gold being found on this mountain.

00:08:01.417 --> 00:08:02.750
Senior?

00:08:03.458 --> 00:08:05.667
If we do not return soon,

00:08:05.667 --> 00:08:08.458
the owner of the
pension will get angry at us.

00:08:08.458 --> 00:08:10.542
Okay! I understand! Gotcha!

00:08:10.542 --> 00:08:14.417
But still, why can't Hatchan
swim a little more energetically?

00:08:29.625 --> 00:08:32.167
Emergency food...

00:08:32.167 --> 00:08:34.542
We must make her tasty.

00:08:46.958 --> 00:08:48.583
"Yukimi Pension"

00:08:49.167 --> 00:08:51.250
We are sorry that we are late!

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:52.917
Terribly sorry.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:56.375
That was a very long break.

00:08:56.375 --> 00:08:59.500
Yes, well, we almost
got lost in the snow, so...

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.833
The bed making and
cleaning are already done.

00:09:01.833 --> 00:09:03.167
What?

00:09:03.958 --> 00:09:05.542
What about you?

00:09:05.542 --> 00:09:10.167
I was kinda thinking of
going to shop for supplies now...

00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:11.833
I see. Then...

00:09:12.792 --> 00:09:14.875
Owner, this is?

00:09:14.875 --> 00:09:16.667
Stocking up on food supplies.

00:09:16.667 --> 00:09:20.958
Our pension prides itself
on its freshness. Meat.

00:09:20.958 --> 00:09:24.333
Wild boar, bears... They're in
the neighborhood, so good luck.

00:09:24.333 --> 00:09:25.833
That means...

00:09:25.833 --> 00:09:28.542
...we have to hunt our own food?

00:09:28.542 --> 00:09:29.667
Is that a "no"?

00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:31.375
I-I'm going now!

00:09:31.875 --> 00:09:34.375
We take the wrong road,
our engine stalls,

00:09:34.375 --> 00:09:37.458
we get a flat tire,
and our car overheats.

00:09:37.458 --> 00:09:40.292
This is getting to be
the best possible scenario.

00:09:40.292 --> 00:09:42.458
Thanks to someone.

00:09:42.458 --> 00:09:44.375
Are you saying
that this is all my fault?!

00:09:44.375 --> 00:09:46.375
It <i>is </i>all your fault!

00:09:50.417 --> 00:09:52.167
"Sure am hungry..."

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:54.542
Hey, in my breast pocket...

00:09:54.542 --> 00:09:55.542
--Hand it over!

00:09:55.542 --> 00:09:57.208
--Why should I?!
--Hand it over!

00:09:57.208 --> 00:09:58.875
Because it's your fault!

00:09:58.875 --> 00:10:01.250
That has nothing to do with--

00:10:06.375 --> 00:10:08.125
They're so late.

00:10:08.875 --> 00:10:10.375
That guy...

00:10:10.375 --> 00:10:12.958
Then that means, this place is...

00:10:13.667 --> 00:10:15.167
"We're right in front of it."

00:10:18.667 --> 00:10:20.875
Aren't you rather inconsiderate
to make such a commotion

00:10:20.875 --> 00:10:22.333
in front of the entrance at night?

00:10:22.333 --> 00:10:23.417
You are?

00:10:23.417 --> 00:10:27.375
Might you be the remaining
members who were late?

00:10:27.375 --> 00:10:31.000
I see. I guess that means
we're colleagues, starting today.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.333
I am...

00:10:32.917 --> 00:10:34.583
Don't repeat the same pattern.

00:10:34.583 --> 00:10:35.750
"Pardon me"
"Director"

00:10:36.208 --> 00:10:39.917
By the way, why is this
guy sleeping on the ground?

00:10:39.917 --> 00:10:42.917
Maybe he likes the
great outdoors. Later.

00:10:45.083 --> 00:10:48.458
Well, who cares?
We finally made it here somehow.

00:10:50.208 --> 00:10:52.292
Misaki Matsuya...

00:10:52.292 --> 00:10:54.125
I've decided!

00:10:54.125 --> 00:10:57.417
She'll be my...
my partner in world peace!

00:10:57.417 --> 00:10:59.333
"He's deciding this all on his own."

00:10:59.667 --> 00:11:01.708
Just leave him alone.

00:11:12.458 --> 00:11:13.625
It's no good.

00:11:13.625 --> 00:11:16.333
I can't fight the innocent
sparkle in their eyes.

00:11:16.333 --> 00:11:18.833
My finger won't move.

00:11:18.833 --> 00:11:21.625
But it's starting to snow more now.

00:11:21.625 --> 00:11:23.292
If I could just get one animal

00:11:23.292 --> 00:11:26.500
before my body becomes
a monument of snow.

00:11:27.958 --> 00:11:29.625
Gotcha!

00:11:35.292 --> 00:11:37.833
M-Menchi!

00:11:40.958 --> 00:11:44.125
Sorry, Will, would you put
her through the reset cycle?

00:11:44.125 --> 00:11:45.333
Yes, dear.

00:11:46.042 --> 00:11:47.208
--One Menchi coming right up!

00:11:47.208 --> 00:11:48.208
--Okay!
--One Menchi coming right up!

00:11:48.208 --> 00:11:49.708
Hey, it's kind of warm.

00:11:49.708 --> 00:11:51.208
All right, done!

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.500
What?!

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.583
You're the one who
brought Menchi along?

00:11:55.583 --> 00:11:57.833
Yes. After all, she is
our emergency food supply.

00:11:57.833 --> 00:12:00.500
I thought that we should
always carry her around with us.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.458
Since you didn't
come back until morning,

00:12:02.458 --> 00:12:04.917
you must have been
stalking a great prey indeed.

00:12:04.917 --> 00:12:06.292
Yo, Owner!

00:12:06.292 --> 00:12:08.333
I almost got lost in
the snow again, that's why!

00:12:08.333 --> 00:12:10.583
The prey? Is this it?

00:12:11.875 --> 00:12:14.167
I haven't done dog in a long while,

00:12:14.167 --> 00:12:17.167
but with the 4,000-year-old
skills honed in Sichuan, China...

00:12:17.167 --> 00:12:18.917
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:12:18.917 --> 00:12:21.583
This is actually our
emergency food supply.

00:12:21.583 --> 00:12:23.917
I see. Well, I suppose
it can't be helped.

00:12:23.917 --> 00:12:27.375
But what a cute dog.
Want some milk?

00:12:27.375 --> 00:12:29.542
And what about our meal?

00:12:29.542 --> 00:12:30.542
Oh, you don't get any.

00:12:30.542 --> 00:12:32.042
I knew it.

00:12:32.792 --> 00:12:37.083
At this rate, we might really have
to resort to Menchi by tomorrow.

00:12:37.083 --> 00:12:38.375
Hatchan, what's this?

00:12:38.375 --> 00:12:40.875
Lord Ilpalazzo
told me to bring this out

00:12:40.875 --> 00:12:43.708
when the story neared the climax.

00:12:43.708 --> 00:12:45.542
Lord Ilpalazzo did?!

00:12:45.542 --> 00:12:47.042
What could it be?

00:12:47.042 --> 00:12:50.292
Wonderful, luxurious
emergency food! What else?!

00:12:50.292 --> 00:12:51.833
Off it comes!

00:12:51.833 --> 00:12:53.292
What is this?

00:12:53.292 --> 00:12:54.792
Attention to all
in-service training students.

00:12:54.792 --> 00:12:56.417
Attention to all
in-service training students.

00:12:56.417 --> 00:12:58.750
Change into your prescribed
uniforms in the locker room

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.750
and immediately gather on
the training grounds.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.917
What?! Locker room?!

00:13:02.917 --> 00:13:04.833
What? You're suddenly
full of enthusiasm.

00:13:04.833 --> 00:13:06.208
"Totally pumped."

00:13:06.208 --> 00:13:08.083
Didn't you hear
what he just said?

00:13:08.083 --> 00:13:09.875
We're changing! We're changing!

00:13:09.875 --> 00:13:11.458
If we sneak in now, we could...

00:13:11.458 --> 00:13:14.875
...we could see the forbidden
nude body of Misaki Matsuya!

00:13:14.875 --> 00:13:17.750
You refer to me so familiarly,
using my full name,

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:19.333
along with words
like changing and nude.

00:13:19.333 --> 00:13:20.833
See ya, Iwata.

00:13:21.417 --> 00:13:25.375
That is, so and so and so forth,
and draw a circle with two dots.

00:13:25.375 --> 00:13:26.667
The sweet and painful balance

00:13:26.667 --> 00:13:29.000
between male psychology
and male physiology fell apart

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.375
and my eloquence and willingness
to talk and work couldn't help it.

00:13:31.375 --> 00:13:32.667
And consider it an impassioned cry...

00:13:32.667 --> 00:13:35.333
Oh, you <i>are </i>going to hit me! I see!

00:13:36.417 --> 00:13:41.208
Well, I don't care what
you do to that idiot, but... well...

00:13:41.208 --> 00:13:42.458
You can call me Matsuya.

00:13:42.458 --> 00:13:45.000
Then, Matsuya,
what's with that outfit?

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.167
It seems to be something
the company special ordered,

00:13:47.167 --> 00:13:49.250
though it's against my inclinations.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:56.625
It's getting old.

00:13:56.625 --> 00:14:00.083
Do we have to wear that Tight,
Totally Revealing Body Suit too?

00:14:00.083 --> 00:14:00.833
"How embarrassing..."

00:14:00.833 --> 00:14:03.625
I wish you wouldn't give it
such an embarrassing name,

00:14:03.625 --> 00:14:05.292
but you'll probably
be wearing them too.

00:14:05.292 --> 00:14:06.625
I don't wanna.

00:14:06.625 --> 00:14:11.208
I don't wanna wear such a Tight,
Totally Revealing Body Suit!

00:14:11.208 --> 00:14:13.583
It doesn't look good on guys!
Not on guys!

00:14:13.583 --> 00:14:15.083
Don't come near me!

00:14:16.042 --> 00:14:19.792
I want you two to carry out
a top-secret mission for me.

00:14:19.792 --> 00:14:22.833
Set up the equipment in this
package on top of the mountain.

00:14:22.833 --> 00:14:26.083
Set the target as the city.
I wish you luck.

00:14:26.083 --> 00:14:29.875
I don't know how this
is related to resources,

00:14:29.875 --> 00:14:34.625
but well, it's for
Lord Ilpalazzo. Right, Hatchan?

00:14:34.625 --> 00:14:36.333
Senior,

00:14:36.333 --> 00:14:38.208
I... death...

00:14:39.333 --> 00:14:43.417
There you go, dying a
sober and yet suitable death!

00:14:44.167 --> 00:14:45.667
On fire!

00:14:47.042 --> 00:14:50.542
Please, Hatchan, do something
about your habit of dying!

00:14:50.542 --> 00:14:52.375
But this is no
time to be complaining!

00:14:52.375 --> 00:14:54.958
Revival plan, part two!

00:14:54.958 --> 00:14:56.500
Wait for me, Hatchan.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.417
I'll warm you right up.

00:15:03.292 --> 00:15:05.000
Hatchan...

00:15:08.042 --> 00:15:12.042
"In Process of Revival"

00:15:12.417 --> 00:15:15.375
Senior, are you okay?
Those frost burns...

00:15:15.375 --> 00:15:18.708
If you really mean that, don't die on
me so easily, okay, Hatchan?

00:15:18.708 --> 00:15:20.542
Or else, I'll end up dead!

00:15:20.542 --> 00:15:20.875
"Do not enter"

00:15:24.458 --> 00:15:26.917
Well, for today's training,

00:15:26.917 --> 00:15:29.500
since all of you made
it through school,

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:32.000
I dare say that there is
no need for an explanation.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.917
Therefore, I will just accept questions.

00:15:33.917 --> 00:15:35.042
Instructor!

00:15:35.042 --> 00:15:36.375
If you do not have any questions...

00:15:36.375 --> 00:15:37.708
Bastard! He ignored me!

00:15:37.708 --> 00:15:39.417
Professor, I have a question.

00:15:39.417 --> 00:15:40.917
What might that be?

00:15:42.792 --> 00:15:43.417
--Professor, my question is this.

00:15:43.417 --> 00:15:45.000
--This is exhausting.
--Professor, my question is this.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.750
This thing that we have in our hands...

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:50.583
You could not even fool a
child if you sold it at a fair booth.

00:15:50.583 --> 00:15:52.667
What is this toy wannabe thing?

00:15:52.667 --> 00:15:54.083
It is a gun.

00:15:54.083 --> 00:15:56.833
Question. What are those
things lined up over there

00:15:56.833 --> 00:16:00.000
that you wouldn't even see at
shooting gallery fair booths?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.583
They are targets.

00:16:01.583 --> 00:16:05.917
Target, schmarget. Besides,
usually, on the first day of work,

00:16:05.917 --> 00:16:08.750
you'd have just a little welcome party.

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:10.917
You are local government employees.

00:16:12.583 --> 00:16:14.708
What's wrong with Watanabe?

00:16:14.708 --> 00:16:17.583
He's just foundering in the
gap between his ideal and reality.

00:16:17.583 --> 00:16:20.375
He'll probably eventually
recalibrate his brain.

00:16:20.375 --> 00:16:23.750
But does this gun really fire bullets?

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.750
It's lighter than a pinball gun.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:28.917
Such questions are best
addressed to the developer.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:45.750
Do... not... po... int... it... at... people?

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:47.667
Considering how seriously he ran away,

00:16:47.667 --> 00:16:50.333
it seems like this thing is
actually not so silly after all.

00:16:50.333 --> 00:16:51.333
"Looks like."

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.583
Camp Three, can you hear me?

00:16:53.583 --> 00:16:55.833
The weather is at its worst.
The temperature is at its lowest.

00:16:55.833 --> 00:16:58.125
The danger is increasing.
But still, I will keep on trying!

00:16:58.125 --> 00:16:59.333
--After all, it's my mission, over.

00:16:59.333 --> 00:17:01.958
--Senior Excel, please be safe, over.
--After all, it's my mission, over.

00:17:01.958 --> 00:17:04.292
And here I am, falling! Over!

00:17:06.625 --> 00:17:09.917
I guess they must
not feed you much at all.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:17.792
My friend left this behind
when he passed away.

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:21.792
Well, it's already
been a long time since then.

00:17:22.875 --> 00:17:27.458
Antonio, I messed up at the very end.

00:17:28.708 --> 00:17:32.250
Please, put me out of my misery.

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:35.375
It's my last request.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.167
Antonio!

00:17:41.917 --> 00:17:44.042
It's that gun.

00:17:44.042 --> 00:17:48.875
That was the last time I pulled a trigger.

00:17:48.875 --> 00:17:50.917
It's an old story.

00:17:53.042 --> 00:17:55.792
So, this is where
you've been hiding out.

00:17:55.792 --> 00:17:57.542
Y-You are...

00:17:57.542 --> 00:17:58.958
...Nabeshin!

00:18:00.542 --> 00:18:04.875
I have succeeded in reaching
the summit on my 324th attack.

00:18:04.875 --> 00:18:08.208
In other words, I fell 323 times.

00:18:08.208 --> 00:18:10.125
Congratulations, Miss Excel!

00:18:10.125 --> 00:18:11.708
Thank you very much.

00:18:11.708 --> 00:18:12.917
How are you feeling?

00:18:12.917 --> 00:18:14.375
The air's thin.

00:18:14.375 --> 00:18:15.292
Any comments?

00:18:15.292 --> 00:18:16.292
It's the pits.

00:18:16.292 --> 00:18:17.375
Are you all right?

00:18:17.375 --> 00:18:18.917
Doesn't look so good.

00:18:19.625 --> 00:18:22.167
I've already reached my limit.

00:18:22.167 --> 00:18:24.542
Excel? Excel?

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:29.042
Excel, I look forward to your success.

00:18:30.042 --> 00:18:33.833
Lord Ilpalazzo!
I'm gonna work hard now!

00:18:33.833 --> 00:18:35.583
Set it up roughly like that.

00:18:36.417 --> 00:18:38.167
Now, push it.

00:18:38.167 --> 00:18:42.167
And show the power of
ACROSS to the ignorant masses!

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:47.167
Show them the murderous power of
our colored laser's sonic wave!

00:18:51.542 --> 00:18:54.708
Now we can complete
the conquest of the city briskly.

00:18:54.708 --> 00:18:56.667
Briskly being the key word here.

00:18:56.667 --> 00:19:00.625
But still, why do we need
to go through target practice?

00:19:00.917 --> 00:19:03.500
"We're supposed to be local
government employees."

00:19:03.792 --> 00:19:06.167
Well, don't think about it too much.

00:19:06.167 --> 00:19:08.833
Let's do it quickly,
eat quickly, and go to sleep.

00:19:08.833 --> 00:19:10.583
That's for the good of justice too.

00:19:11.417 --> 00:19:15.458
I'm going to shoot! To protect
the future peace of the citizenry!

00:19:27.875 --> 00:19:31.125
No!

00:19:37.958 --> 00:19:42.500
J-Just now, did a weird colored
beam-looking laser shoot out?

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:45.667
How the hell do you
get an effect like that?

00:19:45.667 --> 00:19:46.792
Professor...

00:19:46.792 --> 00:19:48.792
I will take one question at a time.

00:19:48.792 --> 00:19:49.500
Sir!

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.375
What is this gun?

00:19:51.375 --> 00:19:53.333
It is a laser gun!

00:19:53.333 --> 00:19:56.500
I'm sure you've seen something like
them in entertainment films.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:59.958
Basically, our current technology
has caught up to fiction.

00:19:59.958 --> 00:20:02.250
The current equipment
that you have been supplied with

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:05.292
is all tentative equipment,
meant only for training.

00:20:05.292 --> 00:20:07.292
In particular, the guns
are an experimental model

00:20:07.292 --> 00:20:09.625
and their power output
is extremely unstable.

00:20:09.625 --> 00:20:12.625
So it turned out to be a bit of
an awkward training session. Sorry!

00:20:12.625 --> 00:20:15.292
So, that's it for today's training!
Dismissed!

00:20:15.292 --> 00:20:16.625
Later!

00:20:18.167 --> 00:20:18.708
What was with that?

00:20:18.708 --> 00:20:21.000
"He seemed to be in an awful rush."

00:20:21.958 --> 00:20:23.667
The ground's rumbling.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:28.458
Avalanche!

00:20:28.458 --> 00:20:29.083
"Yup..."

00:20:31.375 --> 00:20:31.833
"Aaah!"

00:20:32.667 --> 00:20:35.000
I will tell you straight, right now!

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.500
Shake off the past!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.875
Now is the time for you to...

00:20:49.375 --> 00:20:50.875
I'm alive.

00:20:50.875 --> 00:20:52.208
I am...

00:20:55.875 --> 00:20:58.083
Looks like you
made it too, Menchi.

00:20:58.833 --> 00:21:00.542
By the way, Hatchan?

00:21:00.542 --> 00:21:01.750
Yes?

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:03.333
Where are we?

00:21:03.333 --> 00:21:04.833
Who knows?

00:21:07.875 --> 00:21:10.250
And so,

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:13.000
my life was taken
in a distant, foreign land

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.542
and I lived in a mysterious
space with strange beings.

00:21:15.542 --> 00:21:17.542
And when I had
finally made it back home,

00:21:17.542 --> 00:21:20.917
my wife had taken to a friend's bed!

00:21:20.917 --> 00:21:24.250
I-I can't stand a life like this!

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:26.542
This is... This is your fault,

00:21:26.542 --> 00:21:28.250
Gomez!

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:30.500
That voice!

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:32.875
Are you Pedro?!

00:21:37.917 --> 00:21:39.417
We made it home.

00:21:39.417 --> 00:21:41.208
"Truly a miracle."

00:21:45.417 --> 00:21:47.667
Oh? You people...

00:21:47.667 --> 00:21:50.083
P-Please, give us something to eat.

00:21:50.083 --> 00:21:51.083
"For the love of God..."

00:21:51.083 --> 00:21:52.958
You're tougher than you look.

00:21:52.958 --> 00:21:54.333
I'm surprised you're alive.

00:21:54.333 --> 00:21:56.083
Misaki Matsuya...

00:21:58.333 --> 00:22:00.000
Iwata...

00:22:03.208 --> 00:22:05.875
I told you not to call me by my full name.

00:22:20.583 --> 00:22:25.458
"Episode 6: The Cold is Winter!
~Snowed Under Episode~"

00:22:25.458 --> 00:22:27.125
"Today's Experiment..."

00:22:27.125 --> 00:22:29.125
"Today's Experiment... Failed"

00:22:50.917 --> 00:22:59.333
<i>I knew, ever since that day</i>

00:22:59.333 --> 00:23:06.750
<i>The reason you had approached me</i>

00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:14.833
<i>Tender and soft</i>

00:23:14.833 --> 00:23:23.625
<i>That my body is to your taste</i>

00:23:24.583 --> 00:23:32.375
<i>To your hunger-stricken eyes</i>

00:23:32.375 --> 00:23:40.250
<i>How does my body seem</i>

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:48.125
<i>If you are to eat me, do it in one blow</i>

00:23:48.125 --> 00:23:56.875
<i>So that the meat does not get hard</i>

00:23:59.458 --> 00:24:01.250
At the cross section of a major
street in F City, F Prefecture,

00:24:01.250 --> 00:24:02.458
if you turn right, then take a
left at the second alley,

00:24:02.458 --> 00:24:04.792
then right, left, right, right,
there is a fancy little hotel.

00:24:04.792 --> 00:24:06.083
Its name is the Ilpalazzo.

00:24:06.083 --> 00:24:07.792
It's a name I've heard somewhere,
but I don't let it bother me.

00:24:07.792 --> 00:24:09.083
The problem is not the name,

00:24:09.083 --> 00:24:11.458
but the smaller than regulation
size manhole behind the hotel.

00:24:11.458 --> 00:24:13.125
According to the information
of Block 3's Mr. Tamai,

00:24:13.125 --> 00:24:16.542
a sound like a beast's cry can
be heard nightly from the manhole.

00:24:16.542 --> 00:24:17.917
It's probably an abandoned
alligator or something.

00:24:17.917 --> 00:24:19.042
There's no reason to bother with it,

00:24:19.042 --> 00:24:20.417
but since it bothers me,
I try going inside.

00:24:20.417 --> 00:24:22.167
Wow! It's gotten to be
a pretty terrible situation!

00:24:22.167 --> 00:24:23.333
Quack Experimental Anime,
Excel Saga.

00:24:23.333 --> 00:24:24.792
Next time:
"Melody of the Underground Passage"

00:24:24.792 --> 00:24:28.594
A reunion between sewer rats has
a strong odor and stings your nose.
